        ("Items 1, 2, 3, 4 are pushed in that order. In what order do they come out when popped repeatedly?", ["1 2 3 4", "4 1 2 3", "2 1 4 3", "4 3 2 1"], 3, "A stack returns items in the reverse of the order they were pushed."),
        ("What happens when you pop from an empty stack?", ["Overflow: the stack grows", "It returns the last value pushed", "Underflow: there is nothing to remove", "The stack is sorted"], 2, "Popping an empty stack is an underflow error."),
        ("What happens when you push onto a full fixed-capacity stack?", ["Underflow", "The oldest item is returned", "Overflow: there is no room for the item", "The top item is replaced silently"], 2, "Pushing onto a full stack is an overflow error."),
