        ("What does the call stack of a running program store?", ["Only the program's source code", "All data of the heap", "The files on disk", "Data for active function calls, such as local variables and return addresses"], 3, "Each function call adds a frame to the stack, and it is removed when the call ends."),
        ("Which feature is naturally built with a stack?", ["A printer waiting line", "Undo in a text editor", "A ticket line at a counter", "A round-robin scheduler"], 1, "The most recent action is the first one undone, which matches last in, first out."),
        ("In Python, which list methods let a list work as a stack?", ["insert(0, x) and remove()", "sort() and reverse()", "index() and count()", "append() to push and pop() to pop"], 3, "append() adds to the end and pop() removes from the end, both in constant time."),
        ("In an array-based stack, what does the 'top' index track?", ["The position of the first item pushed", "The position of the most recently pushed item", "The total capacity", "The middle of the array"], 1, "push increases top and pop decreases it."),
